1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,900
In 1878,

2
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:02,820
Anandibai Joshee's infant

3
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:04,801
son died after just ten days.

4
00:00:05,421 --> 00:00:06,521
She believed better medical

5
00:00:06,561 --> 00:00:07,541
care might have saved him.

6
00:00:08,121 --> 00:00:09,061
His death helped shape

7
00:00:09,081 --> 00:00:10,041
a decision that would take

8
00:00:10,061 --> 00:00:11,201
her thousands of miles

9
00:00:11,241 --> 00:00:12,642
from India: she wanted

10
00:00:12,662 --> 00:00:13,982
to study medicine in the United

11
00:00:14,022 --> 00:00:15,342
States and become a doctor.

12
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:17,142
Joshee had a particular

13
00:00:17,182 --> 00:00:17,542
purpose.

14
00:00:18,122 --> 00:00:18,962
Some women in India

15
00:00:19,022 --> 00:00:20,063
would not accept treatment

16
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:20,923
from male physicians.

17
00:00:21,443 --> 00:00:22,283
She wanted to be able

18
00:00:22,303 --> 00:00:23,663
to treat those women herself.

19
00:00:24,403 --> 00:00:26,563
On February 24, 1883,

20
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,164
Joshee publicly explained

21
00:00:28,204 --> 00:00:29,784
her plan in Serampore, India.

22
00:00:30,324 --> 00:00:31,244
She addressed concerns

23
00:00:31,284 --> 00:00:32,544
about women studying medicine

24
00:00:32,844 --> 00:00:33,784
and about her intention

25
00:00:33,804 --> 00:00:34,724
to travel overseas.

26
00:00:35,345 --> 00:00:35,905
She acknowledged

27
00:00:35,945 --> 00:00:36,705
that some medical

28
00:00:36,725 --> 00:00:37,845
instruction was available

29
00:00:37,865 --> 00:00:39,165
in India, but considered

30
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:40,485
it inadequate for the thorough

31
00:00:40,545 --> 00:00:41,325
training she wanted.

32
00:00:41,885 --> 00:00:42,585
She also hoped

33
00:00:42,605 --> 00:00:43,466
to return with medical

34
00:00:43,506 --> 00:00:44,546
knowledge and establish

35
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:45,486
instruction for women.

36
00:00:46,106 --> 00:00:47,586
Travel raised another concern.

37
00:00:48,126 --> 00:00:49,266
Going overseas could lead

38
00:00:49,306 --> 00:00:50,707
to exclusion from her religious

39
00:00:50,767 --> 00:00:51,627
and social community.

40
00:00:52,207 --> 00:00:53,527
Joshee intended to remain

41
00:00:53,547 --> 00:00:54,887
Hindu, keep her customs,

42
00:00:55,127 --> 00:00:56,047
and return to India.

43
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:57,467
Her husband supported

44
00:00:57,487 --> 00:00:58,808
her education and expected

45
00:00:58,848 --> 00:00:59,388
to send money.

46
00:00:59,988 --> 00:01:00,688
By late June,

47
00:01:00,948 --> 00:01:01,708
Joshee had reached

48
00:01:01,788 --> 00:01:02,708
Roselle, New Jersey.

49
00:01:03,168 --> 00:01:03,688
But crossing

50
00:01:03,708 --> 00:01:05,128
the ocean had not yet secured

51
00:01:05,168 --> 00:01:05,628
her a place

52
00:01:05,668 --> 00:01:06,429
at a medical college.

53
00:01:07,029 --> 00:01:09,529
On June 28, 1883, she wrote

54
00:01:09,549 --> 00:01:10,709
to the Woman's Medical College

55
00:01:10,729 --> 00:01:12,229
of Pennsylvania in Philadelphia,

56
00:01:12,549 --> 00:01:13,769
seeking admission on terms

57
00:01:13,809 --> 00:01:14,410
she could afford.

58
00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:15,650
She had seventy

59
00:01:15,670 --> 00:01:17,010
dollars and expected twenty

60
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:17,630
dollars a month

61
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:19,210
from her husband, less the cost

62
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:20,110
of transferring the money.

63
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:22,151
By October, she was enrolled

64
00:01:22,171 --> 00:01:23,491
in Philadelphia.

65
00:01:23,611 --> 00:01:25,331
In 1884, Joshee suffered

66
00:01:25,371 --> 00:01:26,631
diphtheria and struggled

67
00:01:26,651 --> 00:01:27,751
to obtain familiar food.

68
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:29,511
Rachel Bodley, the dean

69
00:01:29,531 --> 00:01:30,312
of the medical college,

70
00:01:30,592 --> 00:01:31,452
helped her with housing

71
00:01:31,532 --> 00:01:32,292
and familiar food.

72
00:01:32,852 --> 00:01:34,232
Joshee lived in Bodley's home

73
00:01:34,272 --> 00:01:35,432
for the remainder of her stay

74
00:01:35,492 --> 00:01:36,152
in Philadelphia.

75
00:01:36,732 --> 00:01:37,993
Joshee continued her studies

76
00:01:38,113 --> 00:01:39,373
and completed five terms.

77
00:01:39,953 --> 00:01:42,133
In March 1886, she graduated

78
00:01:42,173 --> 00:01:43,073
from the Woman's Medical

79
00:01:43,113 --> 00:01:44,173
College of Pennsylvania.

80
00:01:44,693 --> 00:01:45,254
Her thesis

81
00:01:45,294 --> 00:01:46,334
concerned obstetrics,

82
00:01:46,674 --> 00:01:47,814
the branch of medicine dealing

83
00:01:47,834 --> 00:01:49,174
with pregnancy and childbirth.

84
00:01:49,754 --> 00:01:50,634
She became the first

85
00:01:50,694 --> 00:01:51,434
woman from India

86
00:01:51,494 --> 00:01:52,734
to earn a degree in Western

87
00:01:52,774 --> 00:01:54,015
medicine in the United States.

88
00:01:54,695 --> 00:01:56,215
After graduation, she pursued

89
00:01:56,315 --> 00:01:57,515
further training, beginning

90
00:01:57,555 --> 00:01:58,635
a six-month internship

91
00:01:58,735 --> 00:01:59,735
at New England Hospital.

92
00:02:00,275 --> 00:02:01,516
Illness forced her to leave

93
00:02:01,576 --> 00:02:02,576
before she could complete it.

94
00:02:03,096 --> 00:02:03,376
She then

95
00:02:03,416 --> 00:02:04,316
accepted an appointment

96
00:02:04,356 --> 00:02:05,976
in India as physician in charge

97
00:02:05,996 --> 00:02:07,336
of the women's ward at Albert

98
00:02:07,416 --> 00:02:08,737
Edward Hospital in Kolhapur.

99
00:02:09,137 --> 00:02:10,277
In October 1886,

100
00:02:10,997 --> 00:02:12,257
Joshee sailed for India.

101
00:02:12,837 --> 00:02:13,877
She arrived in November,

102
00:02:14,337 --> 00:02:15,057
seriously ill.

103
00:02:15,717 --> 00:02:17,918
On February 26, 1887,

104
00:02:18,278 --> 00:02:20,098
Anandibai Joshee died in Pune.

105
00:02:20,738 --> 00:02:21,738
She had earned her medical

106
00:02:21,778 --> 00:02:23,258
degree, accepted a hospital

107
00:02:23,278 --> 00:02:24,519
appointment, and returned

108
00:02:24,539 --> 00:02:25,079
to the country

109
00:02:25,119 --> 00:02:26,119
where she hoped to serve.

110
00:02:26,679 --> 00:02:27,319
But she died

111
00:02:27,359 --> 00:02:28,159
before she could begin

112
00:02:28,219 --> 00:02:29,239
practicing medicine there.

